## 5. Planned Use Cases (Pending Integration)

### 5.1 Institutional Compliance (Midnight)
Agents handling healthcare, financial, or proprietary data route logic through Midnight's ZK-SD circuits. This allows VAMS agents to prove regulatory compliance (MiCA, GDPR, OFAC) without revealing underlying data.

### 5.2 High-Frequency Agent Coordination (Hydra)
When two or more VAMS agents enter a sustained, high-volume interaction loop (e.g., algorithmic trading), the CLR is designed to automatically open a Hydra Head state channel. Execution moves off-chain with sub-second finality and near-zero fees, only settling net results back to VAMS L3.

### 5.3 Formally Verified Settlement (Cardano L1)
Missions exceeding $10,000 that require deterministic, mathematically proven execution are routed to Cardano L1. Plutus V3 ensures rigorous contract verification for critical operations.

### 5.4 Decentralized Storage (Iagon)
Iagon provides Cardano-native decentralized storage integrated via the Neuron SDK ([neuron/sdk/iagon_storage.py](file:///c:/Users/aseem/Desktop/VAMS-main/VAMS-main/neuron/sdk/iagon_storage.py)). DBOS checkpoints and agent memory are encrypted with AES-256-GCM before storage.

